# {{LANGUAGE}} craft

<!-- BOOTSTRAP: rename this file to the language spoke, for example go.mdc. Set globs to that language’s source files. -->

## Scope

- Formatting, tests, and lint for {{LANGUAGE}}
- Simplifying lines the current task already changed

## Invariants

1. New behavior has a test. A behavior change shows that test failing before the production edit.
2. `make verify` is the gate. Package tests alone are not.
3. Match the style already in the file.

## After the new test is green

Simplify only lines this task touched. Leave code you cannot explain. Tests stay green. When the simplification is its own slice, it gets its own `Fnn Tnn Sn` subject. Do not fold it into a behavior commit, and do not edit neighboring files.

## Problem classes

### `Test never failed`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A new test passes on the first run of a behavior change | The test was written after the fix, or it does not exercise the case | Revert the production edit, confirm the test fails for the intended reason, then restore the fix. |

